  "scope": "Font.encodeXRF directly calls xgeFontBuildXRFMemory, adopting an exact resident-XRT allocation through the generic int-count bytes output contract. Original native serialization/cache semantics, no C business wrapper or native change.",
  "performanceBoundary": "Native copies atlas pages into each XRF blob. Language admission makes no additional payload copy but creates one byte-value shell. Each warmed 100-call sample in C and language uses 200 allocations/frees and zero reallocations; common checked scopes, ownership, cold caches and CPU time remain separate costs.",
